---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
import { homeContent } from '../data/home';
const { photos } = homeContent;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Toby McGuire — software developer"
>
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-surface-900">
        <img
          src={photos.icon}
          alt="Toby McGuire profile photo"
          class="inline-block w-12 h-12 mr-2 rounded-full object-cover"
        />
        About Me
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-lg">
          I'm Toby McGuire, a developer who builds both software and games. I
          like working across the life cycle of a problem, from concept to completion. 
        </p>

        <p>
          On the software side, my biggest strength is in my adaptability. I'm used to
          diving into massive, complex codebases and quickly finding my footing. Recently,
          I've been focused on growing my full-stack skills through projects like
          Cookbook, a recipe organization app that touches everything from
          frontend UI to backend architecture, and creating this portfolio site.
        </p>

        <p>
          On the game dev side, I build with C# and Unity. My biggest project
          right now is Sumo, a multiplayer fighting game that started as a small
          prototype on itch.io and grew into something heading for Steam. Working on it has
          taught me a lot about real-time networking, game polish, and shipping
          something that feels complete.
        </p>
          
        <p>
          Outside of programming I enjoy running, the outdoors, and spending time with my cats.
          I've run in a couple marathons and am training for more.
        </p>

        <p>
          I've also published several games on itch.io: puzzle games,
          platformers, survival games, each one a chance to explore a different
          corner of game design and development.
        </p>

        <p>
          I care about clean code, clear architecture, and building things that
          work well. I'm always learning, always building, and always looking for
          the next interesting problem to solve.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 float-center align-middle place-items-center">
        <img
          src={photos.marathon}
          alt="Toby running a marathon"
          class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-cover rounded-lg"
        />
        <img
          src={photos.vab}
          alt="Toby at the Vehicle Assembly Building"
          class="w-full aspect-[4/4] object-cover rounded-lg"
        />
        <img
          src={photos.cats}
          alt="Toby's cats"
          class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-cover rounded-lg"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a
          href={siteConfig.github}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 text-surface-700 font-medium hover:bg-surface-100 transition-colors text-sm"
        >
          GitHub
        </a>
        <a
          href={siteConfig.itch}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 text-surface-700 font-medium hover:bg-surface-100 transition-colors text-sm"
        >
          itch.io
        </a>
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-primary-600 text-white font-medium hover:bg-primary-700 transition-colors text-sm"
        >
          Get in Touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
